From: Roshan Gautam <roshangautam07@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:24:57 +0545
Subject: [PATCH 67/74] deps,build,test: fix array index hash collision

This enables v8_enable_seeded_array_index_hash and adds a test for it.

Strings that look like array indices (decimal integers up to 2^24-1 with
at most kMaxCachedArrayIndexLength digits) store the integer itself in
the 24-bit value field of Name::raw_hash_field, unseeded. The string
table, name dictionaries etc. probe on the low bits of that hash, so an
attacker who can get chosen numeric strings internalized (e.g. via
JSON.parse of a request body) can build arbitrarily long probe chains
and cause O(n^2) behaviour. The fix stores a seeded, invertible
permutation of the value instead, keyed by per-process random secrets.

Fixes: https://hackerone.com/reports/3511792
Refs: https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/march-2026-hashdos
CVE-ID: CVE-2026-21717

This is a backport to V8 10.2 of the Node.js 20 fix (nodejs/node commit
af5c144ebc, nodejs-private/node-private#834), which is a squash of:

