Backport-Notes:
  - V8 10.2 has no rapidhash string hasher (strings are still hashed with
    the seeded Jenkins one-at-a-time hash, as in Node.js 20). As upstream
    did for Node.js 20, third_party/rapidhash-v8 is imported verbatim only
    to derive the three secrets (rapidhash_make_secret) from which the
    multipliers m1..m3 and their inverses are taken. The regular string
    hash continues to use only the 64-bit seed.
  - HashSeed is a view over the hash_seed ByteArray as upstream, but it
    holds a byte pointer and reads fields with base::ReadUnalignedValue.
    Upstream allocates the ByteArray kDoubleAligned and casts it to the
    struct; in 10.2 neither FactoryBase::NewByteArray/AllocateRawArray take
    an alignment nor does the read-only deserializer preserve one (ByteArray
    payloads are only tagged-size aligned, i.e. 4 bytes with pointer
    compression), so the NewByteArray/AllocateRawArray alignment plumbing
    from 185f0fe09b72 was not ported. HashSeed::Data still defines the
    layout and the CSA offsets (the 32-bit multiplier fields used by
    generated code are always 4-byte aligned). HashSeed::secret() takes an
    index instead of returning a pointer for the same reason.
    HashSeed::InitializeRoots() builds the Data on the stack and copy_in()s
    it, CHECKing that the ByteArray has the expected size.
  - CSA SeedArrayIndexValue/UnseedArrayIndexValue use Int32Mul on Word32
    (Uint32Mul does not exist in 10.2); the low 32 bits of the product are
    identical.
  - ReadOnlyHeap::GetReadOnlyRoots() (no argument) is added only under
    V8_SHARED_RO_HEAP, as upstream. AstRawString::AsArrayIndex uses it when
    V8_SHARED_RO_HEAP is defined (the default Node.js 18 configuration);
    otherwise (--experimental-enable-pointer-compression or
    --disable-shared-ro-heap) it falls back to re-parsing the at most
    7 digit literal, which is what it already did for longer index strings.
    Upstream does not compile without V8_SHARED_RO_HEAP.
  - 10.2 uses FLAG_hash_seed instead of v8_flags.hash_seed, HeapObject::
    GetReadOnlyRoots() instead of EarlyGetReadOnlyRoots(), and has no
    shared-heap-deserializer comment to update.
  - kZeroHashSeed users (runtime.cc, wasm-engine.cc x2, strings-storage.cc,
    heap-snapshot-generator-inl.h, debug-interface.cc) use
    HashSeed::Default(); its seed() is 0, so their non-index hashes are
    unchanged. test/fuzzer/regexp-builtins.cc likewise uses
    HashSeed::Default() instead of its private constant seed.
  - GN: V8_USE_DEFAULT_HASHER_SECRET is added to the "features" config
    (=1/=0) rather than to external_v8_defines/v8-gn.h, which 10.2 does
    not generate the same way. In the gyp build it is left undefined (as in
    the Node.js 20 fix), which selects randomly generated secrets.
  - BUILD.bazel/.gitignore/src/DEPS updated for parity; DEPS only needs the
    hash-seed.cc rule since heap.cc and string-hasher-inl.h do not include
    rapidhash here.
  - tools/make-v8.sh: same EXTRA_V8_OPTS as upstream minus
    v8_enable_static_roots, which does not exist in V8 10.2.
  - cctest updates as upstream (test-strings incl. the new
    ArrayIndexHashRoundTrip test, test-heap, test-serialize,
    test-code-stub-assembler). These are not built by the Node.js gyp
    build and were not compiled.
  - v8_embedder_string bumped by one for this single combined backport.

